TIP:  A pretty song to fingerpick, especially on the lower register.  Below are the opening notes.  The numbers refer to open strings unless specified.  Paul picks the intro using a D chord shape on the 10th fret but it's easier to pick the G shape down in the 3rd.  This only applies when untransposed.

Part 1:  2 - 3 - 4 - 4th string/2nd fret - 3.                        The notes are:  b - g - d - e - g
Part 2:  2 - 3 - 4 - 4th string/2nd fret.                             The notes are:  b - g - d - e
Part 3:  2 - 3 - 4 - 4th string/2nd fret - 3.                        The notes are:  b - g - d - e - g
Part 4:  3rd string/2nd fret - 3 - 4th string/4th fret - 3     The notes are:  a - g - f# - f

TIP:  The first word in each verse is held for two counts.  That's what the ... means.

TIP:  (Fmaj7) isn't played too often.  Play it like you're going to play a regular (F) but don't barre the bottom string.  Or like you're going to play a (C) but drop the top two fingers down one extra string. 

     
